		<title type="html"><![CDATA[LCD display and backlight]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2013&amp;p=16971#p16971"><![CDATA[
The LCD display has the same usable resolution as the GD77/DM1801, 128 x 64 pixels, however the phyical display aspect ratio is more rectangular than the GD77, and the pixels are rectangular rather than square<br><br>This is very obvious on the satellite polar screen, which draws a circle, becuase the circle looks like an elipse.<br><br>We are using the bitmap fonts, and this results in the text looking more bold than on the GD88, and much more bold than the official firmware font.<br><br>We may be able to make some minor adjusments to the bitmap font, but I don't personally have a problem with the font being more bold, and I think the official font is less readable, so we are not likely to make any major changes to the font.<br><br>It may be possible to slighly correct the satellite polar display, but its also not a big problem, and it is more readable being eleptical.<br><br><br><br>The backlight intensity is not adjustable in the official firmware, but I have tried to make it adjustable in this firmware, like on the GD77.<br><br>However, there are some limitations to this because we can only use relatively low frequency of PWM as the display electronics do not seem able to handle frequencies above a few hundred Hertz.<br><br>There is also a strange problem when selecting very low display backlight levels, e.g. 2 or 3% because the hardware seems to not like very small short pulses of PWM<br><br>Also on some radios if you listen carefully the PWM signal can be heard on Tx. But it is inaudible on most radios, so is not a big problem, and there is no possible firmware solution to this<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Mon Jan 03, 2022 12:19 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
